This is not normal behaviour. When you are blind your intrinsic 
telepathy should override the 'warning' power of the Orb of Fate, so you 
always get the best possible combination of effects.
I can however think of an explanation for what you experience, but 
telling you this will spoil you about things that you (if this is the 
case) obviously have not yet found out about the game.


* PROBABLY SPOILY EXPLANATION *


You might not have deduced that your telepathy is limited in that it 
will only tell you of monsters 'with a mind'. So if you are 
telepathic+blind+warned you will not see these monsters until the 
warning kicks in - *if* it does, since warning only shows 'non-trivial' 
monsters.
Drop/hide the Orb and be just blind+telepathic and you will notice that 
some monsters will not show up at all.
Noone said this was an easy game, right? ;) Even if you were lucky to be 
telepathic and having a great artifact.
If you are playing with the standard tiles the color of the question-
mark will indicate how dangerous the monster is relative to you, or 
switch to ASCII mode and you will get easier-to-interpret digits, with 
the higher digit the more danger.

> Is there any way to disable
> this "feature" of the Orb of Fate?

As you learned from the above, there is no negative effect of the Orb 
happening here. Rather it is making things a bit better for you when you 
blindly encounter monsters which aren't telepathically perceivable.

